ith Parent's consent; (ix) changes in accounting standards or Law; (x) changes in the price or trading volume of the Company's stock, in and of itself; (xi) any failure to meet financial projections or expectations; and (xii) Transaction Litigation; provided further, that with respect to clauses (i) through (vi) and (ix), such Effects shall be taken into account if they disproportionately affect the Company compared to others in the industry. (Pages 12-13)\nAnswer:
